  "answer": "Honey bee colonies collapse primarily due to Varroa mites (a parasitic mite), pesticide exposure, and diseases like deformed wing virus. These factors cause mass die-offs of worker bees while leaving queen bees and brood behind, leading to colony collapse disorder (CCD) in regions such as North America and Europe. The process is exacerbated by poor hive management and climate change impacts on bee health."
